From: Kodi visionOS port
Subject: [PATCH] videotoolbox: exclude OpenGL ES pixel buffer keys on visionOS

visionOS (TARGET_OS_XR) sets TARGET_OS_IPHONE=1 but does not export
kCVPixelBufferOpenGLESCompatibilityKey (iOS/tvOS only) or
kCVPixelBufferIOSurfaceOpenGLTextureCompatibilityKey (macOS only); both
symbols are marked API_UNAVAILABLE(visionos) and the compiler emits a
hard error.

Guard both branches with !TARGET_OS_XR so visionOS skips both keys
entirely.  VideoToolbox on visionOS does not need either hint: it uses
IOSurface natively via CVMetalTextureCache without any OpenGL bridge.

diff --git a/libavcodec/videotoolbox.c b/libavcodec/videotoolbox.c
--- a/libavcodec/videotoolbox.c
+++ b/libavcodec/videotoolbox.c
@@ -820,7 +820,7 @@ static CFDictionaryRef videotoolbox_buffer_attributes_create(int width,
     CFDictionarySetValue(buffer_attributes, kCVPixelBufferWidthKey, w);
     CFDictionarySetValue(buffer_attributes, kCVPixelBufferHeightKey, h);
-#if TARGET_OS_IPHONE
+#if TARGET_OS_IPHONE && !TARGET_OS_XR
     CFDictionarySetValue(buffer_attributes, kCVPixelBufferOpenGLESCompatibilityKey, kCFBooleanTrue);
-#else
+#elif !TARGET_OS_XR
     CFDictionarySetValue(buffer_attributes, kCVPixelBufferIOSurfaceOpenGLTextureCompatibilityKey, kCFBooleanTrue);
